# Explicit firmware package list for the cham3 M1 desktop image (F2, owner-approved).
#
# This list replaces live-build's automatic firmware selection
# (--firmware-chroot true in earlier revisions). That selection installs every
# package whose Contents entry lists a path under lib/firmware, which includes
# firmware-b43-installer and firmware-b43legacy-installer. Their postinst scripts
# download Broadcom firmware from GitHub and OpenWrt while the image is built and
# fail the build when those hosts are not reachable. They are deliberately not
# listed: Broadcom b43 and b43legacy SoftMAC wireless adapters are not supported
# out of the box (an explicit, owner-approved reduction). brcmfmac and brcmsmac
# firmware (firmware-brcm80211) is present. On an installed system with network
# access, "apt install firmware-b43-installer" remains available to a user.
#
# The 42 names are the previous automatic selection for amd64 (47 packages from
# the main, contrib, non-free and non-free-firmware indices, plus firmware-linux,
# minus the two b43 installers and the ARM-only packages firmware-qcom-soc,
# firmware-samsung, firmware-ti-connectivity and raspi-firmware). Every package is
# fetched from the signed Debian archive. Five of them are not Wi-Fi firmware
# (indi-dsi, libsbig4t64, libfishcamp1t64, alsa-topology-conf, wireless-regdb) and
# are kept only to preserve the previous hardware coverage.
#
# Source: docs/research/M1_package_disposition.md section 6 and
# docs/research/evidence/firmware/proposed_set_without_b43_installers_42.txt.
# --firmware-binary stays true (installer-side firmware). Its selection covers the
# --archive-areas of auto/config; contrib, the only area holding the b43 installers, is
# supplied through config/archives/cham3_debian_contrib.list instead, so the installer
# payload holds the same 42 names (F7). tests/run_tests.sh image-m1 checks the ISO pool
# and /firmware of the built image for the b43 installers and for these names.
alsa-topology-conf
amd64-microcode
atmel-firmware
bluez-firmware
dahdi-firmware-nonfree
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-ast
firmware-ath9k-htc
firmware-atheros
firmware-bnx2
firmware-bnx2x
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-carl9170
firmware-cavium
firmware-cirrus
firmware-intel-graphics
firmware-intel-misc
firmware-intel-sound
firmware-ipw2x00
firmware-ivtv
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-libertas
firmware-linux
firmware-linux-free
firmware-marvell-prestera
firmware-mediatek
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-myricom
firmware-netronome
firmware-netxen
firmware-nvidia-graphics
firmware-nvidia-tesla-535-gsp
firmware-qlogic
firmware-realtek
firmware-siano
firmware-sof-signed
firmware-zd1211
indi-dsi
intel-microcode
libfishcamp1t64
libsbig4t64
wireless-regdb
